---
/**
 * Template preview route (§17): the inner-page template with realistic
 * service-shaped placeholder content — long headings, H3 cards, bullets,
 * both required inline CTAs, alert list, included panel, post-body sections.
 * noindex; excluded from nav and sitemaps. Never Lorem Ipsum.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import InnerPageTemplate from '../../components/templates/InnerPageTemplate.astro';
import InlineCTA from '../../components/InlineCTA.astro';
import ContentAlertList from '../../components/ContentAlertList.astro';
import IncludedPanel from '../../components/IncludedPanel.astro';
import InnerSubsections from '../../components/InnerSubsections.astro';
import ProcessStepper from '../../components/ProcessStepper.astro';
import ReviewSection from '../../components/ReviewSection.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../../components/FinalCTA.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Template preview — inner page"
  description="Internal inner-page template preview."
  noindex
>
  <InnerPageTemplate
    heroEyebrow="Water Damage Restoration"
    h1="Water Damage Cleanup and Structural Drying in Example City"
    heroIntro="Standing water spreads into walls, flooring, and framing within hours. Our crews extract, dry, and document the damage — and stay with you through the rebuild."
    parentHub={{ label: 'Water Damage Services', url: '/water-damage-restoration/' }}
    current={{ label: 'Water Damage Cleanup', url: '/water-damage-restoration/water-damage-cleanup/' }}
    relatedNav={[
      { label: 'Flood Damage Restoration', url: '/water-damage-restoration/flood-damage/' },
      { label: 'Sewage Cleanup', url: '/water-damage-restoration/sewage-cleanup/' },
      { label: 'Burst Pipe Cleanup', url: '/water-damage-restoration/burst-pipe/' },
      { label: 'Basement Flooding', url: '/water-damage-restoration/basement-flooding/' },
      { label: 'Structural Drying', url: '/water-damage-restoration/structural-drying/' },
      { label: 'Appliance Leak Cleanup', url: '/water-damage-restoration/appliance-leak/' },
    ]}
    coreHubs={[
      { label: 'Water Damage Restoration', url: '/water-damage-restoration/' },
      { label: 'Fire Damage Restoration', url: '/fire-damage-restoration/' },
      { label: 'Mold Remediation', url: '/mold-remediation/' },
      { label: 'Storm Damage Restoration', url: '/storm-damage-restoration/' },
      { label: 'Reconstruction', url: '/reconstruction/' },
    ]}
  >
    <h2>Emergency water damage cleanup for homes and businesses</h2>
    <p>
      When water gets where it shouldn't be, the first hours decide how much of your property can
      be saved. Drywall wicks moisture upward, subfloors swell, and hidden cavities stay wet long
      after the surface looks dry. Our certified technicians respond {site.emergencyAvailability},
      extract standing water fast, and set up professional drying equipment the same visit.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every step is documented — moisture readings, photos, and scope notes — so your insurance
      claim is supported from day one and nothing gets argued about later.
    </p>

    <InlineCTA
      heading="Standing water right now?"
      support="Call immediately — extraction within hours is the difference between drying and demolition."
    />

    <h2>Signs you need professional water damage cleanup</h2>
    <p>
      Not all water damage announces itself. If you notice any of the following, the damage is
      usually further along than it looks:
    </p>

    <ContentAlertList
      alerts={[
        { title: 'Buckling or cupping floors', text: 'Moisture trapped in or under the flooring.' },
        { title: 'Musty smell that returns', text: 'Often the first sign of hidden moisture or early mold.' },
        { title: 'Stains spreading on walls or ceilings', text: 'Active leaks travel along framing before they show.' },
        { title: 'Peeling paint or bubbling drywall', text: 'Wall cavities holding water behind the surface.' },
      ]}
    />

    <h2>What our water damage cleanup service includes</h2>
    <p>
      One crew, one scope, start to finish. A typical cleanup engagement covers everything from
      the first extraction through verified dry-out:
    </p>

    <IncludedPanel
      heading="Included in every cleanup"
      items={[
        'Emergency water extraction',
        'Moisture mapping and readings',
        'Commercial dehumidification',
        'Antimicrobial treatment',
        'Contents protection and packout',
        'Daily drying checks',
        'Insurance-ready documentation',
        'Rebuild coordination',
      ]}
    />

    <h3>How long does drying take?</h3>
    <p>
      Most structures dry in three to five days with professional equipment — far faster than the
      weeks an untreated space can take, and without the mold risk. We verify with moisture meters
      rather than guessing by look or feel, and we don't pull equipment until the numbers say dry.
    </p>

    <h2>Related water damage services</h2>

    <InnerSubsections
      items={[
        { title: 'Sewage Cleanup', text: 'Category 3 water needs containment and disinfection, not just drying.', url: '/water-damage-restoration/sewage-cleanup/' },
        { title: 'Basement Flooding', text: 'Below-grade water brings its own extraction and drying challenges.', url: '/water-damage-restoration/basement-flooding/' },
        { title: 'Burst Pipe Cleanup', text: 'Supply-line failures can release hundreds of gallons in minutes.', url: '/water-damage-restoration/burst-pipe/' },
        { title: 'Structural Drying', text: 'Verified dry-out for framing, subfloors, and wall cavities.', url: '/water-damage-restoration/structural-drying/' },
      ]}
    />

    <p>
      Whatever the source — storm, plumbing failure, appliance leak, or flood — the goal is the
      same: stop the spread, dry the structure, prove it with documentation, and put your property
      back the way it was.
    </p>

    <InlineCTA
      heading="Need water damage cleanup help now?"
      support="One call starts extraction, drying, and documentation — we handle the rest."
    />

    <Fragment slot="post-body">
    <ProcessStepper
      eyebrow="Simple process"
      heading="What happens after you call"
      steps={[
        { title: 'Call anytime', text: 'A real person answers, asks the right questions, and dispatches a crew.' },
        { title: 'Extract & dry', text: 'Standing water out, drying equipment in, moisture documented daily.' },
        { title: 'Restore & rebuild', text: 'From verified dry-out through reconstruction, one team finishes the job.' },
      ]}
    />
    <ReviewSection
      eyebrow="What our customers say"
      heading={`Property owners trust ${site.name}`}
      intro="Every review comes straight from the platforms our customers use."
    />
    <FinalCTA
      heading="Don't Wait — Water Spreads Every Hour"
      support="The sooner extraction starts, the more we can save. Call now and talk to a real person."
    />
    </Fragment>
  </InnerPageTemplate>
</BaseLayout>
